# What each command of tools/ci/correctness.tests costs a hosted runner, for `parallel --shard K/N --costs`
# (docs/commands/parallel.md): its time times the CPUs it held there (its heading's, at most the runner's 4), in
# seconds, then its title as its heading has it. The hosted test job deals the inventory to its shards by these, the
# costliest first, each to the shard whose commands cost the least so far; a command without a line costs its CPUs
# times 10 s, and a line whose title the list doesn't have is left out. The costs only balance the shards, never select
# what runs: a stale cost makes a shard longer, not a test go missing. Refresh them from a hosted run's report (each
# heading's time, times its CPUs up to 4) when the shards' times drift apart.
#
# From run 41519216885's plain rows, its shards' reports (the mean of its x86-64 and native times), 2026-11-02. The
# sanitizer rows take these too, so their shards balance only roughly. The last two lines are from run 41543634134,
# for commands main added since.
